{
  "answer": "The product is a moderate skin irritant, eye irritant, and may cause respiratory irritation. It can also be irritating to mucous membranes in the nose, throat, and lungs. Ingestion of excessive amounts may cause headache, nausea, abdominal pain, vomiting, and diarrhea.",
  "source": "SECTION 7-HEALTH HAZARDS AND FIRST AID"
}

{
  "answer": "Wear rubber gloves, chemical splash goggles, and protective outerwear when handling. Avoid contact with eyes, skin, and clothing. Avoid breathing of vapors or mists. Use in well-ventilated area. Keep out of reach of children. For use by trained personnel only.",
  "source": "SECTION 6-STORAGE AND HANDLING INFORMATION"
}

{
  "answer": "Get to fresh air. Seek medical attention if irritation persists.",
  "source": "SECTION 9-SPILL OR LEAK PROCEDURES"
}

{
  "answer": "Flush with water. Seek medical attention if irritation persists.",
  "source": "SECTION 7-HEALTH HAZARDS AND FIRST AID, First Aid Procedures"
}

{
  "answer": "Immediately flush with large quantities of water, holding eyelids open. Seek medical attention if irritation persists.",
  "source": "SECTION 7-HEALTH HAZARDS AND FIRST AID"
}

{
  "answer": "Do not induce vomiting. Drink large quantities of water. Seek medical attention immediately.",
  "source": "SECTION 9-SPILL OR LEAK PROCEDURES, Ingestion"
}

{
  "answer": "Information not available in the provided context",
  "source": "N/A"
}

{
  "answer": "Alkaline vapors",
  "source": "SECTION 4-FIRE AND EXPLOSION HAZARD DATA"
}

{
  "answer": "No special fire handling procedures are required for this product.",
  "source": "SECTION 4-FIRE AND EXPLOSION HAZARD DATA, SECTION 9-SPILL OR LEAK PROCEDURES"
}

{
  "answer": "Floors will become slippery. Avoid walking in product. Keep unessential personnel away. Mop up or otherwise absorb and hold disposal. Avoid discharge to sewer or open waterways. Waste Disposal Method: Any method in accordance with local, state and federal laws. Best method is to recycle or reuse for intended purpose. Consult local authorities for disposal in public sewer. Do not dispose of into storm drain, stream, river or to ground. Rinse container thoroughly before discarding in trash.",
  "source": "SECTION 9-SPILL OR LEAK PROCEDURES"
}

{
  "answer": "To ensure safe handling and storage, wear rubber gloves, chemical splash goggles, and protective outerwear when handling. Avoid contact with eyes, skin, and clothing. Store in a well-ventilated area, keep out of reach of children, and for use by trained personnel only. Keep container closed during storage.",
  "source": "SECTION 6-STORAGE AND HANDLING INFORMATION"
}

{
  "answer": "Use in well-ventilated area, provide local exhaust to keep TLV of Section 2 ingredients below acceptable limit, wear rubber gloves, chemical splash goggles, protective outerwear, and protective rubber footwear when using on floor.",
  "source": "SECTION 6-STORAGE AND HANDLING INFORMATION, SECTION 7-HEALTH HAZARDS AND FIRST AID"
}

{
  "answer": "The product, Revite (Green), is a Heavy Duty Cleaner Degreaser with the following physical and chemical properties: Thin green liquid with characteristic odor; Boiling Point: 212 F; Specific Gravity: 1.055; Flash Point: None (water-based); Vapor Pressure: 20mm Hg @ 68 F; Vapor Density (Air=1): >1; Upper Explosion Limit: N/A; Lower Explosion Limit: N/A; % Volatile: 85+; pH: 12.0 ??13.0; Solubility in Water: Complete; Evaporation Rate (Water=1): <1; VOC Content: 2.93% (wt/wt), 0.26 lbs/gal., 30.9 grams/liter.",
  "source": "SECTION 3-PHYSICAL DATA, SECTION 4-FIRE AND EXPLOSION HAZARD DATA"
}

{
  "answer": "The product is stable, with no hazardous polymerization noted in SECTION 5-REACTIVITY DATA.",
  "source": "SECTION 5-REACTIVITY DATA"
}

{
  "answer": "Alkaline vapors",
  "source": "SECTION 5-REACTIVITY DATA"
}

{
  "answer": "The product contains a toxic chemical, Glycol Ether (CAS# 111-76-2), which is an eye irritant and may cause skin irritation with prolonged or repeated contact. It can also be irritating to the mucous membranes in the nose, throat, and lungs, and ingesting it may cause headache, nausea, abdominal pain, vomiting, and diarrhea. Excessive amounts may cause collapse.",
  "source": "SECTION 6-STORAGE AND HANDLING INFORMATION, SECTION 7-HEALTH HAZARDS AND FIRST AID"
}

{
  "answer": "When handling this product, wear rubber gloves, chemical splash goggles, and protective outerwear. Avoid contact with eyes, skin, and clothing. Work in a well-ventilated area to prevent breathing of vapors or mists. Keep the container closed during storage. For institutional and industrial use only. Use by trained personnel is recommended.",
  "source": "SECTION 6-STORAGE AND HANDLING INFORMATION"
}

{
  "answer": "The product is a moderate skin irritant, eye irritant, and may cause respiratory irritation. Ingestion can lead to headache, nausea, abdominal pain, vomiting, and diarrhea. Excessive amounts may cause collapse. The product also has flammability hazards.",
  "source": "SECTION 7-HEALTH HAZARDS AND FIRST AID, SECTION 4-FIRE AND EXPLOSION HAZARD DATA"
}

{
  "answer": "Respiratory Protection: Vapors and mists may be irritating to mucous membranes in the nose, throat, and lungs. Skin: Moderate skin irritant. Prolonged or repeated contact may cause redness, dermatitis. Eyes: Eye irritant. Liquid and mists will cause tearing, redness, burning sensation. Ingestion: Irritating to the mouth and throat. May cause headache, nausea, abdominal pain, vomiting, and diarrhea. Excessive amounts may cause collapse.",
  "source": "SECTION 7-HEALTH HAZARDS AND FIRST AID"
}

{
  "answer": "Get to fresh air. Seek medical attention if irritation persists.",
  "source": "SECTION 9-SPILL OR LEAK PROCEDURES, SECTION 7-HEALTH HAZARDS AND FIRST AID"
}

{
  "answer": "Flush with water. Seek medical attention if irritation persists.",
  "source": "SECTION 7-HEALTH HAZARDS AND FIRST AID, SECTION 9-SPILL OR LEAK PROCEDURES"
}

{
  "answer": "Immediately flush with large quantities of water, holding eyelids open. Seek medical attention if irritation persists.",
  "source": "SECTION 7-HEALTH HAZARDS AND FIRST AID"
}

{
  "answer": "In case of ingestion, do not induce vomiting. Drink large quantities of water. Seek medical attention immediately.",
  "source": "SECTION 7-HEALTH HAZARDS AND FIRST AID"
}

{
  "answer": "Any method in accordance with local, state and federal laws. Best method is to recycle or reuse for intended purpose. Consult local authorities for disposal in public sewer. Do not dispose of into storm drain, stream, river or to ground.",
  "source": "SECTION 9-SPILL OR LEAK PROCEDURES"
}

{
  "answer": "No specific storage requirements or conditions are mentioned in the SDS.",
  "source": "SECTION 1-PRODUCT IDENTIFICATION AND SUPPLIER INFORMATION, SECTION 10-REGULATORY INFORMATION"
}

